# S-IC retro motor (Thiokol TE-M-424): NASA CEA input deck (RP-1311 free form).
# Run by tools/make_exhaust_table.py; the spec takes the equilibrium
# expansion (a frozen one stops at the throat: its condensed species
# leave their temperature ranges).
#
# Propellant: "ammonium perchlorate oxidizer in a polysulfide fuel binder"
#   (MSFC-MAN-503 p. 4-27, H); its formulation is not given: TP-E-8104,
#   Thiokol's polysulfide-AP of the LES tower jettison motor, stands in (L).
# p,psia: 1,650, Thiokol's nominal at 60 F (AS-501 FER §12.2.1, H; AS-501's
#   telemetry read 1,700-1,850 psia).
# supar: 4.5 (L): the area ratio at which this deck's vacuum thrust
#   coefficient puts the exit of a nozzle delivering 87,000 lbf (AS-501 FER
#   Table 12-2) at 0.9 of the 15.25 in case (MSFC-MAN-503 p. 4-27).
# Propellant: Thiokol TP-E-8104, polysulfide (LP-33) and ammonium
#   perchlorate with 2 % aluminium, by weight (TN D-6295 Table I(a), H). The
#   heats of formation not in CEA's library are the deck's: LP-33 per
#   C5H10O2S2 repeat unit -493 kJ/mol, set so that CEA gives TN D-6295 Table
#   I(b)'s flame temperature, 4,404 F (2,702 K) at 1,000 psia (its chamber
#   gamma then comes out at the table's 1.176, an independent check); GMF
#   (p-quinone dioxime) 0, dibutyl carbitol -640 and diphenylguanidine +140
#   kJ/mol, estimates (L; together 4 % of the mass). Benzyl mercaptan (0 to
#   0.09 %) is left out.
# omit: CEA 3.3.4's equilibrium expansion does not converge past the throat
#   with the spinel MgAl2O4 (0.5 mol % in the chamber), so its Mg and Al go
#   to MgO, MgCl2 and Al2O3.
reac
  fuel=NH4CLO4(I)                                    wt%=72.000 t(k)=298.15
  fuel=AL(cr)                                        wt%=2.000 t(k)=298.15
  fuel=LP-33      C 5 H 10 O 2 S 2 h,kj/mol=-493     wt%=18.810 t(k)=298.15
  fuel=GMF        C 6 H 6 N 2 O 2 h,kj/mol=0         wt%=1.390 t(k)=298.15
  fuel=S(a)                                          wt%=0.010 t(k)=298.15
  fuel=MgO(cr)                                       wt%=1.000 t(k)=298.15
  fuel=Fe2O3(cr)                                     wt%=2.000 t(k)=298.15
  fuel=TP-903     C 12 H 26 O 3 h,kj/mol=-640        wt%=2.090 t(k)=298.15
  fuel=DPG        C 13 H 13 N 3 h,kj/mol=140         wt%=0.700 t(k)=298.15
prob case=S-IC-retro rocket p,psia=1650 eql supar=4.5
omit MgAL2O4(cr) MgAL2O4(L)
output siunits trace=1e-5
end
